 "findings":[
  {"heading":"Epidemic curves","segment_index":"S1.P2","kind":"untrue","en_span":"chapters/epicurves.qmd:17-17","tr_span":"chapters/epicurves.vn.qmd:16-19","proposition":"The Vietnamese states the chapter demonstrates two approaches, the incidence2 package (simple commands) and ggplot2; the English states only that it demonstrates epicurves with ggplot2.","reader_consequence":"A Vietnamese reader expects and looks for an incidence2 section that does not exist anywhere in the chapter, and may believe the omission is a rendering fault or that they skipped it.","confidence":"high"},
  {"heading":"Epidemic curves","segment_index":"S1.P2","kind":"missing","en_span":"chapters/epicurves.qmd:27-27","tr_span":"chapters/epicurves.vn.qmd:26-27","proposition":"The English states that incidence2 was undergoing revisions, was not stable at the time of writing, and will be re-added to the chapter when stable; the Vietnamese omits this entirely.","reader_consequence":"A Vietnamese reader is not warned that incidence2 is unstable, so may adopt it for production epicurve code on the handbook's implied endorsement.","confidence":"high"},
  {"heading":"Packages","segment_index":"S3.P1","kind":"untrue","en_span":"chapters/epicurves.qmd:36-36","tr_span":"chapters/epicurves.vn.qmd:35-35","proposition":"The Vietnamese says library() from base R installs a package (\"cài đặt package với hàm library()\"); the English says library() loads an already-installed package.","reader_consequence":"A Vietnamese reader believes library() will install a missing package, so runs library() on an uninstalled package, gets \"there is no package called ...\", and has no stated route to install it.","confidence":"high"},
  {"heading":"Epicurves with ggplot2","segment_index":"S7.P1","kind":"added","en_span":"chapters/epicurves.qmd:146-146","tr_span":"chapters/epicurves.vn.qmd:136-136","proposition":"The Vietnamese opens the sentence with \"Unlike using the incidence2 package\" (\"Không giống như sử dụng package incidence2\"), asserting a contrast with incidence2 behaviour that the English sentence does not make.","reader_consequence":"A Vietnamese reader infers that incidence2 handles time aggregation and date-axis labelling automatically, a claim the chapter never supports or demonstrates, and may choose incidence2 on that basis.","confidence":"high"},
  {"heading":"Specify case bins","segment_index":"S8.P1","kind":"untrue","en_span":"chapters/epicurves.qmd:180-180","tr_span":"chapters/epicurves.vn.qmd:167-167","proposition":"The Vietnamese says binwidth = is set to the number of bins of the histogram (\"đặt binwidth = bằng số bins của histogram, tính bằng ngày\"); the English says binwidth = sets the width of the histogram bins, in days.","reader_consequence":"A Vietnamese reader sets binwidth to the desired count of bars rather than the bar width in days, producing an epicurve with the wrong time aggregation while the code runs without error.","confidence":"medium"},
  {"heading":"Weekly epicurve example","segment_index":"S9.P1","kind":"missing","en_span":"chapters/epicurves.qmd:280-280","tr_span":"chapters/epicurves.vn.qmd:261-262","proposition":"The English bullet list states that closed = \"left\" is used in geom_histogram() to ensure dates are counted in the correct bins; the Vietnamese bullet list omits this point.","reader_consequence":"A Vietnamese reader building a weekly epicurve does not know to set closed = \"left\", so cases falling exactly on a Monday break are assigned to the previous week and every weekly count near a boundary can be off by those cases.","confidence":"high"},
  {"heading":"Multi-level date labels","segment_index":"S29.P1","kind":"missing","en_span":"chapters/epicurves.qmd:1341-1341","tr_span":"chapters/epicurves.vn.qmd:1248-1250","proposition":"The English states that the easiest method for multi-level date labels is passing scales::label_date_short() to the labels = argument of scale_x_date(), and that its labels adapt automatically as the data span grows from days to weeks to months and years; the Vietnamese omits this paragraph and presents only the faceting method.","reader_consequence":"A Vietnamese reader never learns the simplest solution to the stated problem and instead implements the far more involved facet_grid() workaround, which also forces a geom_area() instead of a histogram.","confidence":"high"},
  {"heading":"Cumulative Incidence","segment_index":"S31.P1","kind":"added","en_span":"chapters/epicurves.qmd:1523-1523","tr_span":"chapters/epicurves.vn.qmd:1414-1414","proposition":"The Vietnamese adds a note that a reader using incidence2 should see the chapter section on computing cumulative incidence with a single simple function, and that this section covers the ggplot() route; the English has no such note.","reader_consequence":"A Vietnamese reader searches the chapter for an incidence2 cumulative-incidence function that is never named or shown, and may abandon the ggplot() method described here while looking for it.","confidence":"high"}
 ]}
